# SQLite durability/safety disabled, or every SQL statement logged. Two related
# better-sqlite3 antipatterns found via mestjs authored ground truth
# (MEST-SQLITE-002, 2026-09-26):
#   - pragma journal_mode=OFF / synchronous=OFF: a crash mid-write corrupts the
#     database — never acceptable for real data (durability traded for "speed").
#   - new Database(..., { verbose: console.log }): logs every SQL statement and
#     its bound parameters to the console/logs — leaks data (CWE-532).
# Both were a false negative: keur had no SQLite-configuration rule.
id: KEUR-SQLITE-001
maturity: 1
title: Unsafe SQLite configuration (durability disabled or SQL logging)
category: security
severity: warning
engine: pattern
action: warn
skip_comments: true
target:
  extensions: .js .ts
patterns:
  - regex: (?i)\.pragma\s*\(\s*['"](?:journal_mode|synchronous)\s*=\s*off['"]
    message: SQLite journal_mode/synchronous set to OFF — durability disabled, a crash mid-write can corrupt the database. Keep the default WAL/NORMAL for real data.
  - regex: new\s+Database\s*\([^)]*verbose\s*:\s*console\.(?:log|info|debug)
    message: SQLite opened with verbose logging to the console — every SQL statement and its bound parameters are logged, leaking data to logs (CWE-532). Remove verbose in production.
confidence: 0.7
fix: Do not disable journal_mode/synchronous for persistent data. Remove the verbose logger, or gate it behind a dev-only check.
